From fe5f43aed6149ddbc3abca6c1262ed2584473a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:29:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] docs(notice): attribute the Simplified-Chinese card text
 and its licence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 大学院废墟 data is CC-BY-SA-4.0 rather than MIT like MTGJSON, so it belongs
in NOTICE rather than only in the generator script's stdout. Records the derived
artifact, the script that produces it, and why the locale cannot come from
MTGJSON's foreignData (Scryfall has no Simplified-Chinese printings).
---
 NOTICE | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/NOTICE b/NOTICE
index cdb1c35f24..284bc1f4b9 100644
--- a/NOTICE
+++ b/NOTICE
@@ -7,3 +7,16 @@ MTGJSON (https://mtgjson.com/)
 Licensed under the MIT License
 Card metadata including names, mana costs, types, oracle text, and other
 game-relevant fields is sourced from MTGJSON's open data sets.
+
+大学院废墟 — magic-cards-zhs (https://github.com/HeliumOctahelide/magic-cards-zhs)
+Licensed under CC-BY-SA-4.0
+Simplified-Chinese card names, Oracle text, and type lines are derived from that
+project's weekly data exports by `scripts/gen-zhs-card-text.mjs`, producing the
+build artifact `client/public/card-data.zhs.json`. Scryfall publishes no
+Simplified-Chinese printings, so this locale cannot come from MTGJSON's
+`foreignData` the way every other content language does.
+
+The derived sidecar is a build output and is not committed; the script that
+produces it, the source revision it reads, and this attribution travel with the
+repository instead.
+
